  "notes": [
    "A HIGH or CRITICAL dangerous pattern without a recorded decision now pauses the commit (`dangerous-pattern-pause [pause]`, \"PAUSE. Architect attention required\"), so the agent stops and asks the Architect instead of landing the pattern behind a printed warning.",
    "The pause has no approval command: it clears when the Architect's decision is recorded in `commit_draft.md`, or when the finding is fixed or removed.",
    "An agent that proceeds without asking must record an explicit skip (`dangerous-pattern-skips`); the commit then carries `Gator-Dangerous-Patterns-Unacknowledged`, shown as \"! Unacknowledged\" in the Commits view.",
    "Every finding key can be recorded: path characters the draft list cannot hold are percent-encoded (`,` becomes `%2C`), and required evidence fails closed in commit-msg, so a commit never lands without its acknowledgement or skip trailers (Codex review).",
    "Charter approval, correctness rules, Enterprise `evidence_only` and the legacy `warn`/`off` levels are unchanged; a commit with both a charter finding and a dangerous pattern needs both the approval and the recorded decision.",
    "The constitution, the warnings and override procedures, the pre-commit checks document, Settings, the resolution contract and the changelog describe the pause.",
